    <!-- Names, pure formats, and the symbol glyphs. A language is called the same thing in
         every locale, a percentage has nothing to translate, and the glyphs stand for keys:
         an abbreviation that changed with the system language would be a second code table to
         learn on a keyboard whose entire cost is memorisation. -->
