    <string name="settings_key_hint">Guide</string>
    <string name="settings_codes">Show the code table</string>
    <string name="settings_codes_note">Every character and what it costs, shortest first. The first dozen cover most of what anyone types.</string>
    <string name="settings_language_note">The language switch cycles through the ones you tick, in this order.</string>
    <string name="settings_language_minimum">At least one language has to stay on.</string>
    <string name="settings_buttons_note">Remotes disagree about which buttons exist and about what they report. Press the button you want and it gets recorded. Nothing here is required: deleting, the caret, the language and the digit layer are all codes on the d-pad. Number keys can be assigned freely — this keyboard never reads them.</string>
    <string name="settings_binding_row">%1$s: %2$s</string>
    <string name="settings_binding_unset">not set</string>
    <string name="settings_system_keyboard">Android keyboard settings</string>
    <string name="settings_system_keyboard_note">Leaves this app. Enable or switch the active keyboard there.</string>
    <string name="settings_check_updates">Check for updates</string>
    <string name="settings_updates_note">The only thing here that uses the network. It runs in a separate process, only when you press it, and sends nothing. What you type never leaves the device.</string>
    <string name="settings_typing_note">Left, right and down are the code symbols: every character is a short run of them, two presses for the common ones and up to six for the rare. The guide above the field shows what each direction leads to from where you are, so you never have to know a code in advance.\n\nUp is reserved and never moves: up-up is space, up-down deletes, up-left goes to the digits, up-right opens the edit mode.\n\nThe digits stay until you press BACK or type a space. In the edit mode, left and right move the caret one character at a time, up deletes, down opens the language list, BACK returns to typing.\n\nCentre submits. BACK drops a half-finished character, then leaves a mode, then closes the keyboard. Nothing needs a long press, and nothing needs a button your remote might not have.</string>
    <string name="settings_scratch_hint">Type here</string>
    <string name="settings_scratch_note">Focus this field to bring the keyboard up. Nothing here is saved.</string>

    <string name="codes_title">Code table</string>
    <string name="codes_intro_shared">One table for every language you have on, built from their letter frequencies together. Frequent characters are cheap, rare ones are not.</string>
    <string name="codes_intro_per_language">One table per language, built from that language\'s own letter frequencies. Frequent characters are cheap, rare ones are not.</string>
